Subject: [PATCH 2/5] Resolve the weight npz paths at call time

what:     frontend/smolvla_e2e.py: the constants MODELS, VISION_NPZ, VLM_NPZ, EXPERT_NPZ become functions models_dir(),
          vision_npz(), vlm_npz(), expert_npz() that read SHVLA_SMOLVLA_DIR when called; the default arguments that bound
          them at import (prepare ckpt, emit_vision, vlm_data, expert_data) become None and are resolved inside (the
          parameters shadow the functions there, so private aliases _vision_npz etc. are used). tests/gvsoc/run.py reads
          E.expert_npz() / E.vlm_npz() instead of E.EXPERT_NPZ / E.VLM_NPZ (run_expert_cost).
why:      a default bound at import keeps the first folder; one process may prepare both checkpoints.
evidence: grep -rn 'MODELS\|VISION_NPZ\|VLM_NPZ\|EXPERT_NPZ' --include=*.py: no use left.
upstream: yes.
applies-to: softhier-mlir b11cd5fa4f3e717374d1e9ba14442ff302d1f970

---
diff --git a/softhier_mlir/frontend/smolvla_e2e.py b/softhier_mlir/frontend/smolvla_e2e.py
index 07042a0..3316393 100644
--- a/softhier_mlir/frontend/smolvla_e2e.py
